# sites.kzp -- the probe plan of the perf-sample observer for profile cfs-v7.0.1 (sub-gate S1-R2,
# Architecture/spec/SPEC_FINAL.md section 9.3).
#
# This file is DATA for `kz anchor` and `kz observe`.  The observer contains no knowledge of the
# framework; everything it knows about the framework is here, each entry with the lines it was read
# from.  The format is the observer's own ("kzp-observe 1", probe/plan/profile.hpp); it is not the
# profile language of the readiness specification (the phi files next to this directory), and it
# does not replace it: the same facts are stated there for the checker, here for the probes.
#
# Source roots: `kz anchor ... --source-root <the pinned bundle>`.  The paths below are relative to
# the bundle's root, as in ../01_prov.kzp, and the sha256 values are those of the cited lines (each
# followed by LF), the value of  sed -n 'A,Bp' FILE | sha256sum.  `kz anchor` recomputes them and
# refuses to build a basis when the text differs.
#
# What each site yields (the four raw slots a0..a3 of an event; kz_raw.h):
#   entry sites   argument registers of the System V x86-64 call at the probed address, which is the
#                 instruction after `endbr64`: the arguments are intact and the word at the top of the
#                 stack is the return address (a3).
#   return sites  the return value (rax) and the instruction pointer, which is the return address.
# The probes sit at function entry (+4): the same address for the entry and the return site.
#
# Nothing here selects a condition of the experiment.  Which sites exist is the plan; the number of
# runs, the stop method and the user are the caller's (docs/observer.md).
#
# Sites 0-7 are the plan of the S1-R2 development run s1r2_p1 (unchanged, so that their ids stay).
# Sites 8-20 (X-03, REV13 change table C-24, W2 2026-10-24) observe the R2 registration and writer
# effects: EVS registration (clear and publish of the slot), the registry linearization point of
# the send function, the AppState raise, and the App-record writers of the core start (memset of
# the ES global, reserve, publish, failure clear).  Sites 21-25 carry the creation-side evidence of
# app_owner (SPEC 1.2 "Creating application", 5.7 items 2 and 4, ADR-056): the start-task request
# with the application it names, the child-task request, and the id the spawn call assigns where it
# passes it to the new thread.  Sites 26-29 (R2 remainder, 2026-10-24) give the location the AppID of the
# send function was read from and the actor that wrote that location: the SB task's store of its own id at
# cfe_sb_task.c:138 as the profile's publication site `sb_publication` (the same instruction as site 2, which
# stays for the counts), and the capture point of the send's value condition at the three SB call sites that
# pass CFE_SB_Global.AppId and that ES and EVS reach before that store (cases/R2.md section 5;
# plan/proof_status_R2.md section 12).  The point sites are named after the linearization points of the
# phi profile (OP.LABEL, or the shared site), so that `kz replay` maps them; plan/proof_status_R2.md
# section 12 is the trace table (site -> source line -> effect -> conjunct).  Every line below was
# re-read in the tree the R2 binary was built from (cFS 088b2fa8, build-native_std; the hashes are
# those of 01_prov.kzp where both cite the same lines).
kzp-observe 1
binary core-cpu1

# ---- cited text ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

